## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a C heap-allocated struct to Go, manage memory explicitly, and keep per-call ownership to avoid data races.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory ownership and explicit free
- Converting C strings with C.GoString
- Per-call memory lifecycle under concurrency
- Error handling when C returns NULL

## Code Example
```c
// header
typedef struct { char name[128]; int age; int active; } UserC;
UserC* fetch_user(int id);
void free_user(UserC*);
```
```go
// Go binding sketch
type User struct { Name string; Age int; Active bool }

// #include "user.h"
import "C"

func GetUserInfo(id int) (User, error) {
  cu := C.fetch_user(C.int(id))
  if cu == nil {
    return User{}, fmt.Errorf("not found")
  }
  u := User{Name: C.GoString(cu.name), Age: int(cu.age), Active: cu.active != 0}
  C.free_user(cu)
  return u, nil
}
```

